From d293cc07f6575eaf9becd1de56c5b79dc2d1afbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:53:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship the vendored nlohmann/json, md5, and rapidyaml licence
 texts

setup.py compiles third_party/json (nlohmann/json, MIT), third_party/md5
(Frank Thilo's MD5 C++ wrapper around the RSA Data Security reference
implementation, a custom permissive notice), and third_party/rapidyaml
(a single-header amalgamation whose MIT notice is embedded as a comment,
not a standalone file) straight into the _jsonnet extension. setup.py
sets only `license="Apache-2.0"` with no license_files/license-files
key anywhere in pyproject.toml or setup.py, so setuptools' default
LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS* root glob is what ships jsonnet's
own LICENSE; it never reaches into third_party/, and the real
jsonnet-0.22.0-cp38-abi3-manylinux_2_24_x86_64.manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
on PyPI carries only that one file under dist-info/licenses/.

third_party/json/LICENSE and third_party/md5/LICENSE already exist;
this reproduces both, byte for byte, at the project root. rapidyaml
ships no separate licence file, so LICENSE.rapidyaml is the MIT notice
extracted verbatim from the comment block in
third_party/rapidyaml/rapidyaml-0.10.0.hpp (the copyright holder's own
wording, unversioned boilerplate). Naming them LICENSE.<dep> at the
root is picked up by the same default glob with no packaging change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not filed against google/jsonnet from this automated port; a maintainer should report it upstream]
---
 LICENSE.md5           | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.nlohmann-json | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.rapidyaml     | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 68 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.md5
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.nlohmann-json
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.rapidyaml

